+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# experts-rega-fine-n-buckets: master's rega sizes each item's wgmma N (tokens) and slab TMA box from the chunk's
+# 16-route block count nbk (1..8) with four buckets (nbk <= 1: 16, <= 2: 32, <= 4: 64, else 128): a chunk of 33-48
+# routes runs N = 64 and one of 65-112 runs N = 128 (up to 3/8 of those items' MMA columns and slab rows padding).
+# A SEPARATE extension muse_prefill_rega_fine, built LAST in prepare(), DERIVED from master's head + body by asserted
+# text edits (each must occur exactly its stated number of times, else no build; master's strings, module, v1
+# fallback and their sha256 checks are untouched) runs N = 16 * nbk: eight Wg<NB> wrappers (NB = 16 .. 128 step 16),
+# eight tensor maps (boxes {64, 16 * (b + 1)}, master's SWIZZLE_128B 2-D map; every box fits the 16 KB slab half;
+# Maps = 1 KB __grid_constant__, static_assert'ed; encoded host-side in rega_gemm_fine as master's rega_gemm does, so
+# at capture, never in a replay), decode_item bucket b = nbk - 1, the producer's tx = WST + 2 * 16 * (b + 1) * 128,
+# an 8-case consumer switch. Dequant, ring, smem layout, epilogue (NB / 8 is even for every NB) and register budget
+# (largest N 128) are master's. A runtime int `fine` picks the mapping inside decode_item, which the producer thread
+# and the consumers both call with the same value (same bucket, box and tx on both sides; a mismatch would still end
+# in master's bounded wait, error word 1, class OFF, never a hang): fine = 1 is N = 16 * nbk; fine = 0 is master's
+# 4-bucket mapping (b = 0 / 1 / 3 / 7) through the same 8-case switch, the OVERHEAD CONTROL (fine-4map vs master =
+# code overhead; fine vs fine-4map = the bucket effect).
+# Per class (low T=753 only with rega_low_variant == 0, high T=3012, ft T=16384): canary through _experts_rega, exact
+# hs / y compare with master's rega_gemm on random, skewed, one and pop routings (on a miss: max |diff| and the first
+# mismatching (class, routing, nbk), then master's fp32-reference calibrated bound as the fallback), 2 interleaved
+# rounds x 11 cold-L2 graph alternations of the three pairs (master, fine-4map, fine) and each kernel alone on the
+# pop and random routings, then (timing pass only) the two-state replay check. ON when fine pair / master pair <= 0.98
+# on pop in both rounds AND <= 1.01 on random (rounds pooled). state['rega_fine_ok'][class] is a plain bool,
+# state['rega_fine_ext'] the module (None when every class is OFF).
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
